      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Drifting away\" means accepting the weight of your history without having to carry it all the time. It doesn't mean giving up, but it means stopping the frantic, exhausting battle against something that feels genetically wired. You can stop trying to *fix* the wiring; instead, you can focus on finding the quietest, least painful way to simply *be* within it. Sometimes the most radical act is just letting go of the need to be 'better' or 'different' than what you've been handed.",
