      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The difference is that fighting is a performance, a desperate, loud effort to convince yourself you matter, and that's draining. Accepting the end, however, is a quiet surrender to the truth of your own nature. If the outcome is set, then the struggle is just noise, and noise is what hurts the most. You don't have to *choose* the end; you can just choose to stop wrestling with the idea of escaping it.",
